From: MeowArchMobile adbd standalone build
Subject: [PATCH] main.cpp: allow FunctionFS USB on non-Android hosts

The USB transport (daemon/usb.cpp) is only excluded from host builds by
Android.bp's target.android srcs — the code itself is plain Linux (kernel
AIO + FunctionFS ioctls + eventfd). Only the usb_init() call site in
adbd_main() is #if defined(__ANDROID__)-guarded; drop the guard so a glibc
adbd picks up /dev/usb-ffs/adb/ep0 when a gadget has been configured.
The access() check makes it a no-op everywhere else.

Regenerated with exact context: the hunk header counted 10 old lines where
the body has 12 (10 context + 2 removals), so patch -N only took it with
fuzz. With fuzz off it failed outright — meaning the guard had silently
never been removed in the working tree.

diff --git a/daemon/main.cpp b/daemon/main.cpp
index 931b170..43f2058 100644
--- a/daemon/main.cpp
+++ b/daemon/main.cpp
@@ -258,13 +265,16 @@ int adbd_main() {
 
     bool is_usb = false;
 
-#if defined(__ANDROID__)
+    // MeowArchMobile: the guard dropped. daemon/usb.cpp is plain Linux (kernel
+    // AIO + FunctionFS ioctls + eventfd); only this call site was
+    // #if defined(__ANDROID__), so a glibc adbd never listened on
+    // /dev/usb-ffs/adb/ep0 even with the gadget configured. The access() check
+    // keeps it a no-op where no FunctionFS endpoint exists.
     if (access(USB_FFS_ADB_EP0, F_OK) == 0) {
         // Listen on USB.
         usb_init();
         is_usb = true;
     }
-#endif
 
     // If one of these properties is set, also listen on that port.
     // If one of the properties isn't set and we couldn't listen on usb, listen
